1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,790
Most people associate virtual reality with the world of gaming or entertainment.
大多数人把虚拟现实与游戏或娱乐领域联系在一起。

2
00:00:04,790 --> 00:00:12,220
What is all the fuss, you may wonder, about a futuristic contraption you wear on your head that makes you look like a creature from Star Wars?
你可能会想，对于一个戴在头上、让你看起来像《星球大战》里的生物的未来派装置，到底有什么大惊小怪的呢？

3
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:20,610
But this emerging technology has been spreading rapidly into many other areas and could fundamentally change your life in the future.
但是这项新兴技术已经迅速传播到许多其他领域，并且在未来可能会从根本上改变你的生活。

4
00:00:20,610 --> 00:00:34,670
Virtual reality, or VR, is a computer-generated technology that creates a three-dimensional digital world that you can not only see and observe, but explore and interact with it as if you are there.
虚拟现实，简称VR，是一种由计算机生成的技术，它创造了一个三维数字世界，你不仅可以看到和观察这个世界，还可以探索并与之互动，就好像你身临其境一样。

5
00:00:34,670 --> 00:00:44,180
Once you put on the special equipment - a helmet or goggles with a screen inside or gloves fitted with sensors - you become immersed in the virtual world.
一旦你戴上特殊设备-一个里面有屏幕的头盔或护目镜，或者装有传感器的手套-你就会沉浸在虚拟世界中。

6
00:00:44,180 --> 00:00:49,920
VR now has serious applications in fields as wide-ranging as business and medicine.
VR现在在商业和医学等广泛的领域都有重要应用。

7
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:56,080
VR has already proved effective as a training tool as it simulates real experiences.
VR作为一种培训工具已经被证明是有效的，因为它可以模拟真实的体验。

8
00:00:56,080 --> 00:01:01,600
One simulation programme educates young drivers about the dangers of bad driving.
一个模拟程序可以教育年轻司机不良驾驶的危险性。

9
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:05,820
Participants experience a dangerous car journey and a virtual accident.
参与者会体验一次危险的驾车旅程和一场虚拟事故。

10
00:01:05,820 --> 00:01:09,000
It is now being used to train surgeons.
现在它也被用于培训外科医生。

11
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:27,520
Connor Pierce of Samsung's IT for UK and Ireland thinks it will impinge on all walks of life: "We'll socialise via VR, we will do business via VR, we'll have VR team-meetings, we'll have VR education, museums will have virtual reality experiences...".
三星英国和爱尔兰信息技术部门的康纳·皮尔斯认为它将影响各行各业：“我们将通过VR进行社交，通过VR开展业务，我们会有VR团队会议，我们会有VR教育，博物馆也会有虚拟现实体验……

12
00:01:27,520 --> 00:01:33,270
Its benefits have been felt in the field of psychology and the treatment of mental health patients.
”。它的益处也体现在了心理学领域以及心理健康患者的治疗方面。

13
00:01:33,270 --> 00:01:41,050
Professor Daniel Freeman at the Warnford Hospital in Oxford uses it to treat vertigo and other anxiety disorders.
牛津大学沃恩福德医院的丹尼尔·弗里曼教授用它来治疗眩晕和其他焦虑症。

14
00:01:41,050 --> 00:01:51,080
He explains that by exposing patients to what they fear most in a virtual environment and showing them that nothing bad happens, they can eventually overcome their panic.
他解释说，通过让患者在虚拟环境中面对他们最害怕的东西，并向他们表明不会发生什么坏事，他们最终可以克服恐惧。

15
00:01:51,080 --> 00:01:55,160
In the world of work too, VR may change our lives dramatically.
在工作领域，VR也可能会极大地改变我们的生活。

16
00:01:55,160 --> 00:01:59,910
Working individually at home, we can connect to our colleagues in a virtual space.
在家独自工作时，我们可以在虚拟空间中与同事联系。

17
00:01:59,910 --> 00:02:03,230
We can be at home and at the office at the same time.
我们可以同时在家和在办公室。

18
00:02:03,230 --> 00:02:07,090
For the first time, we can really be in two places at once.
我们第一次真正能够同时身处两个地方。

19
00:02:07,090 --> 00:02:13,960
Some VR developers predict that the impact of VR could be as significant as the internet or mobile phones.
一些VR开发者预测，VR的影响可能会和互联网或手机一样重大。

20
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:19,530
Google alone has sold 2 million cardboard VR headsets in the last two years.
仅谷歌一家公司在过去两年里就售出了200万个纸板VR头戴设备。

21
00:02:19,530 --> 00:02:22,460
Is a new age of reality about to dawn?
一个新的现实时代即将开始吗？
